    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are leaning heavily on the favorable matchup against Adrian Houser today, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Curtis Mead** (62.15) anchoring the lineup. Both benefit significantly from Houser\u2019s high xERA (4.78) and strong tailwinds, which push their efficiency scores well above the threshold for elite starts. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a much tougher test against Logan Gilbert, his elite skill set and the favorable wind conditions at his park keep him as our highest-rated option (74.03). Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** is a strong play at 62.91; his high-quality xwOBA and the leadoff advantage against G. Holmes make him a critical component for both R and SB production today.\n\nThe decision to bench **Nolan Schanuel** (50.89) was the tightest call of the morning, as he performed admirably against Kai-Wei Teng but ultimately fell short of the volume efficiency provided by our starters. We are opting to navigate the difficult matchups against Skenes and Burns with caution; **Kyle Tucker** (48.01), **Jackson Merrill** (53.45), and **Andy Pages** (43.93) are all active, but their scores are dampened by the elite SP skill of their opponents. We are actively monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Nasim Nunez**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, as any shift down the batting order could immediately degrade their efficiency. Lastly, while **Brayan Rocchio** was considered for his SP matchup upside, the 43% rain risk at his venue combined with a projected bottom-of-the-order start kept him on the bench to preserve our game caps.",
